<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6577"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Armchairpi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Armchairpi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 08, 2005 - 1:42 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTW, I&#39;m especially interested in news media or other objective/reliable sources that provide details currently missing from the timeline about the crime scene- eg. whether the telephone line was cut, or the bodies hooded, the car moved, etc..  Please <a href="mailto:armchairpi@yahoo.com">send me</a> links to this kind of information if you come across it.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
