<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6722"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Armchairpi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Armchairpi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 09, 2005 - 12:58 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tom, the goal for the timeline is to collect together info. about the official crimes, BTK communications, and the unsolveds crimes, and present them in an integrated, very terse, and somewhat graphical manner. <BR> <BR>Hopefully it might be a tool to recoginize patterns in the crimes &#40;timing, m.o., etc.&#41;, ex/include crimes from the BTK profile, develop a sense for the BTK&#39;s rhythm, etc.. <BR> <BR>I don&#39;t think the timeline, for instance, would be a good introduction and overview of BTK for the unitiated reader, whereas your History is very good for this. <BR> <BR>Actually, as I keyed in all those cold cases, the patterns really started to jump out; there really seems to be some pretty distinctive groupings: the BTK-like crimes &#40;home invasions, telco cut, car taken, strangulation, etc.&#41;; murders of women with the bodies left in tubs; someone abducting women, raping and murdering them, then dumping the bodies; home invasion murders coupled with arson; etc.. <BR> <BR>Right now, as a result of this timeline exercise, my gut is saying that a lot of the unsovleds sort out into these other patterns, leaving only a few behind that are possibly BTK&#39;s: The Slaughters, Davis, Hedge, and Berardi.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6722-->
<!--Post: 6733--><!--Time: 1107989354-->
